    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "The weather team now wants a linear regression model for humidity based on the hour of the day. This time, the model has not yet been created: you’ll need to create, train, and test the model yourself.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Create a new, untrained linear regression model.\r\n2. Train it on the inputs (hours) and outputs (humidities).\r\n3. Compute the model’s prediction for the humidity at 3 pm (hour 15) and at 11 pm (hour 23) and print each prediction. Then, print the actual humidity recorded in the dataset for 3 pm and 11 pm.\r\n4. Run the program and compare the line with the readings, as in Level 1.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nTo create a new untrained model, call `LinearRegression()` and save the result in a variable.\r\n\r\nUse `model.fit` to train it on a dataset of inputs and outputs.\r\n\r\nThe `humidities` list stores all of the humidities from the training data, sorted by hour. `humidities[0]` is the humidity recorded at midnight.\r\n",
